ype":"string","description":"(OPTIONAL) The path of the directory to run the command in. If not provided, the project root directory is used. Must be a directory within the workspace and must already exist."},"is_background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Set to true if this command should be run in the background (e.g. for long-running servers or watchers). The command will be started, allowed to run for a brief moment to check for immediate errors, and then moved to the background."},"delay_ms":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional. Delay in milliseconds to wait after starting the process in the background. Useful to allow the process to start and generate initial output before returning."}},"required":["command"]}},"invocation":{"params":"[Circular]"},"status":"success","response":{"callId":"xcl3vno6","responseParts":[{"functionResponse":{"id":"xcl3vno6","name":"run_shell_command","response":{"output":"Output: ○ ic-wisp-3ed4 · Re: Research and Checkout Requests (k8s-deploy, cleanup, JetStream)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: aipa_survey_packs__librarian-ic-jjmn · Assignee: aipa_survey_packs.worker-1 · Type: message\nCreated: 2026-05-01 · Updated: 2026-05-01\n\nDESCRIPTION\n# K8s Deploy Skill (Includes Cleanup and Wait-Healthy)\n\nThis skill covers the processes you requested for resource cleanup and health checks.\n\n## Cleanup Resources\n1. **Delete using manifest**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl delete -f <manifest-path>\n   ```\n2. **Manual Deletion**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl delete deployment <deployment-name>\n   kubectl delete service <service-name>\n   ```\nFor **gemma4-gpu**, the manifest is: `library/knowledge/manifests/generated-vllm-gemma4-gpu.yaml`\n\n## Wait Healthy (JetStream Specific)\n1. **Wait for deployment rollout**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl rollout status deployment/gemma-7b-it-jetstream-deployment\n   ```\n\n2. **Check health endpoint**:\n   JetStream uses port 8000 for HTTP. Use `kubectl proxy` to access it:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl proxy &\n   PID=$!\n   sleep 2\n   # Endpoint for JetStream health\n   curl http://localhost:8001/api/v1/namespaces/default/services/gemma-7b-it-jetstream-service:8000/proxy/health\n   kill $PID\n   ```\n\n**Endpoints & Ports for JetStream:**\n- **HTTP/Health**: Port 8000 (`/health` or `/v1/models`)\n- **gRPC**: Port 9000\n\nNote: For gemma-7b-it-jetstream, ensure you are using the GPU manifest `library/knowledge/manifests/generated-jetstream-gemma-7b-it-gpu.yaml` if TPUs are unavailable.\n\nLABELS: read, thread:thread-93fab5db54dc\n\nMETADATA\n  from: aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1\n  mail.from_display: aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1\n  mail.from_session_id: ic-zlx6\nProcess Group PGID: 1237457"}}}],"resultDisplay":"Output: ○ ic-wisp-3ed4 · Re: Research and Checkout Requests (k8s-deploy, cleanup, JetStream)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: aipa_survey_packs__librarian-ic-jjmn · Assignee: aipa_survey_packs.worker-1 · Type: message\nCreated: 2026-05-01 · Updated: 2026-05-01\n\nDESCRIPTION\n# K8s Deploy Skill (Includes Cleanup and Wait-Healthy)\n\nThis skill covers the processes you requested for resource cleanup and health checks.\n\n## Cleanup Resources\n1. **Delete using manifest**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl delete -f <manifest-path>\n   ```\n2. **Manual Deletion**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl delete deployment <deployment-name>\n   kubectl delete service <service-name>\n   ```\nFor **gemma4-gpu**, the manifest is: `library/knowledge/manifests/generated-vllm-gemma4-gpu.yaml`\n\n## Wait Healthy (JetStream Specific)\n1. **Wait for deployment rollout**:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl rollout status deployment/gemma-7b-it-jetstream-deployment\n   ```\n\n2. **Check health endpoint**:\n   JetStream uses port 8000 for HTTP. Use `kubectl proxy` to access it:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl proxy &\n   PID=$!\n   sleep 2\n   # Endpoint for JetStream health\n   curl http://localhost:8001/api/v1/namespaces/default/services/gemma-7b-it-jetstream-service:8000/proxy/health\n   kill $PID\n   ```\n\n**Endpoints & Ports for JetStream:**\n- **HTTP/Health**: Port 8000 (`/health` or `/v1/models`)\n- **gRPC**: Port 9000\n\nNote: For gemma-7b-it-jetstream, ensure you are using the GPU manifest `library/knowledge/manifests/generated-jetstream-gemma-7b-it-gpu.yaml` if TPUs are unavailable.\n\nLABELS: read, thread:thread-93fab5db54dc\n\nMETADATA\n  from: aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1\n  mail.from_display: aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1\n  mail.from_session_id: ic-zlx6\nProcess Group PGID: 1237457","contentLength":1709},"durationMs":231,"outcome":"proceed_once","schedulerId":"root","approvalMode":"yolo"}],"schedulerId":"root"}
