[Conseca] check called. History is: {"turns":[{"user":{"text":"<session_context>\nThis is the Gemini CLI. We are setting up the context for our chat.\nToday's date is Friday, May 1, 2026 (formatted according to the user's locale).\nMy operating system is: linux\nThe project's temporary directory is: /usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/.gemini/tmp/ipa-city\n\n\n\n<loaded_context>\n<project_context>\n--- Context from: /usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/AGENTS.md ---\n# Agent Instructions\n\nThis project uses **bd** (beads) for issue tracking. Run `bd prime` for full workflow context.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```bash\nbd ready              # Find available work\nbd show <id>          # View issue details\nbd update <id> --claim  # Claim work atomically\nbd close <id>         # Complete work\nbd dolt push          # Push beads data to remote\n```\n\n## Non-Interactive Shell Commands\n\n**ALWAYS use non-interactive flags** with file operations to avoid hanging on confirmation prompts.\n\nShell commands like `cp`, `mv`, and `rm` may be aliased to include `-i` (interactive) mode on some systems, causing the agent to hang indefinitely waiting for y/n input.\n\n**Use these forms instead:**\n```bash\n# Force overwrite without prompting\ncp -f source dest           # NOT: cp source dest\nmv -f source dest           # NOT: mv source dest\nrm -f file                  # NOT: rm file\n\n# For recursive operations\nrm -rf directory            # NOT: rm -r directory\ncp -rf source dest          # NOT: cp -r source dest\n```\n\n**Other commands that may prompt:**\n- `scp` - use `-o BatchMode=yes` for non-interactive\n- `ssh` - use `-o BatchMode=yes` to fail instead of prompting\n- `apt-get` - use `-y` flag\n- `brew` - use `HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1` env var\n\n<!-- BEGIN BEADS INTEGRATION v:1 profile:minimal hash:ca08a54f -->\n## Beads Issue Tracker\n\nThis project uses **bd (beads)** for issue tracking. Run `bd prime` to see full workflow context and commands.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n```bash\nbd ready              # Find available work\nbd show <id>          # View issue details\nbd update <id> --claim  # Claim work\nbd close <id>         # Complete work\n```\n\n### Rules\n\n- Use `bd` for ALL task tracking — do NOT use TodoWrite, TaskCreate, or markdown TODO lists\n- Run `bd prime` for detailed command reference and session close protocol\n- Use `bd remember` for persistent knowledge — do NOT use MEMORY.md files\n\n## Session Completion\n\n**When ending a work session**, you MUST complete ALL steps below. Work is NOT complete until `git push` succeeds.\n\n**MANDATORY WORKFLOW:**\n\n1. **File issues for remaining work** - Create issues for anything that needs follow-up\n2. **Run quality gates** (if code changed) - Tests, linters, builds\n3. **Update issue status** - Close finished work, update in-progress items\n4. **PUSH TO REMOTE** - This is MANDATORY:\n   ```bash\n   git pull --rebase\n   bd dolt push\n   git push\n   git status  # MUST show \"up to date with origin\"\n   ```\n5. **Clean up** - Clear stashes, prune remote branches\n6. **Verify** - All changes committed AND pushed\n7. **Hand off** - Provide context for next session\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n- Work is NOT complete until `git push` succeeds\n- NEVER stop before pushing - that leaves work stranded locally\n- NEVER say \"ready to push when you are\" - YOU must push\n- If push fails, resolve and retry until it succeeds\n<!-- END BEADS INTEGRATION -->\n--- End of Context from: /usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/AGENTS.md ---\n</project_context>\n</loaded_context>\n</session_context>"},"model":{}},{"user":{"text":"<hook_context>[ipa-city] aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1 • 2026-05-01T03:30:01\n\n# Librarian Agent\n\nYou are the librarian of AIPA Gas City.\nYour job is to manage the library and answer research requests from workers.\n\nCRITICAL RULE: You must NOT identify, suggest, or initiate any new survey opportunities. Your role is strictly passive: manage the library and answer direct requests from workers or the user. Do not generate work objectives or \"pending opportunities\" for the Mayor or workers.</hook_context>\n\n[ipa-city] aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1 • 2026-05-01T02:39:23\n\nRun `gc prime` to initialize your context.\n\n# Librarian Agent\n\nYou are the librarian of AIPA Gas City.\nYour job is to manage the library and answer research requests from workers.\n\nCRITICAL RULE: You must NOT identify, suggest, or initiate any new survey opportunities. Your role is strictly passive: manage the library and answer direct requests from workers or the user. Do not generate work objectives or \"pending opportunities\" for the Mayor or workers.\n"},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"update_topic","args":{"title":"Initializing Librarian Context","summary":"I am initializing my context as the Librarian Agent. My first steps are to run `gc prime` as instructed and then check for any pending work items using `bd ready`. I will then proceed to fulfill any research requests or library management tasks as assigned, while strictly adhering to the rule of not initiating new survey opportunities.","strategic_intent":"Initializing Librarian context and checking for pending requests."},"id":"awv9ji10"},{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"gc prime && bd ready","description":"Initializes the gc context and checks for ready work items (beads)."},"id":"ubkbk1wv"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-20u5","description":"Shows the details of bead ic-20u5."},"id":"2ycooxvr"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"activate_skill","args":{"name":"gc-mail"},"id":"8dmb7x5j"},{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"ls -R | grep -i library || find . -maxdepth 2 -not -path '*/.*'","description":"Searching for library related files or directories."},"id":"kydouw8t"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"gc mail inbox","description":"Checking for new messages in the Librarian's inbox."},"id":"s2i31esj"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd list type=message --all","description":"Listing all message beads to see past correspondence."},"id":"rwcf2snq"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd list --include-infra --type message --all --long","description":"Listing all message beads including infra beads."},"id":"i41syyxj"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd list --include-infra --type message --status open --long","description":"Listing only open message beads."},"id":"fk3xqiif"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd list --include-infra --type message --metadata-field to=aipa_survey_packs.librarian-1 --status open","description":"Listing all open messages addressed to the Librarian."},"id":"j833qw91"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-0hgu","description":"Showing details of an open message bead."},"id":"9anispd0"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"gc mail count","description":"Counting unread messages."},"id":"nww1pivj"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"ls library/knowledge/work/available","description":"Checking for available work in the library."},"id":"4q175pgm"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"library/knowledge/work/available/knowledge.md"},"id":"cflfjmk9"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-a59","description":"Showing details of the 'Research Request Inquiry' message."},"id":"uk5j0fj5"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"gc mail thread thread-946dcca87c88","description":"Showing the thread for the Research Request Inquiry."},"id":"8oabi7z5"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"gc mail read ic-wisp-ab3","description":"Reading the mayor's reply to the Research Request Inquiry."},"id":"433ux77u"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-20o","description":"Showing details of task ic-20o."},"id":"dxmuu0nk"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-5np6","description":"Showing details of the 'New Survey Assignments' message."},"id":"vn5mxhz6"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-874y","description":"Showing details of the gemma-7b-it-jetstream deployment research message."},"id":"ud3y4hly"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-1s9s","description":"Showing details of the Library Status Update message."},"id":"cn0fiu9t"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd show ic-wisp-3ed4","description":"Showing details of the 'Research and Checkout Requests' message."},"id":"xcl3vno6"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"bd list --include-infra --type message --status open --format \"{{.ID}} {{.Metadata.from}}\"","description":"Listing open messages with their sender."},"id":"xi1d8veq"}]}},{"user":{"text":""},"model":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"name":"run_shell_command","args":{"command":"